            <ArticleTitle>Glomus tumor of the nasal vestibulum: a rare clinical presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>112-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5606/kbbihtisas.2012.021</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">kbbihtisas.2012.021</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glomus tumor is an uncommon benign tumor rising from the glomus bodies. It is most often found on limbs and rarely involve the head and neck. In this report, we present the 31st documented case of a intranasal glomus (nasal vestibular) tumor, an extremely rare localization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
